            <ArticleTitle>Military rubella.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1273-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An epidemic of rubella in 46 young adults occurred. Detailed descriptions of clinical signs and symptoms, basic laboratory evaluation and serologic investigation are provided. None of the vaccinees who became ill lacked IgM antibody. An interesting clinical observation was the 25% incidence of testicular pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
